    "15:א": "(1) (sec. 10) The Lulav 20. II in the p. of the Tos. Ral 4 L7, mentioned there in Shas Din, made a house of his own and gave in it the Lulav Dach, the author of the name of Raba's words, they were distah dalkih by DA Shema Lakiha. And from the second Raba, such as they brought out in the vessel and the crucible of the Shas, and the saying Raba for taking by DA, it is called for taking. Not by holding the sides of the vessel, but placing his hand under its rim. Or they held the hand of the vessel of the Akal HaToh. And per the 2nd of the words of the Tos and Zal Rabbi the Rabbi does not hold the dofni of the Meiri vessel. In the Gemara, it is used in the Gemara because it is a buffer (and it is not crisp and the Ham Raba Lekiha by the DA calls it Lekiha. Does the MM not come out as a buffer) but by placing his hand under the edge of the vessel. The vessel does not come out.",
    "15:ב": "(2) And the head of the MS, etc., in a hollow barrel and held RL hold onto the lulav that the lulav reaches to the end of the barrel. Dai does not hold onto the lulav only the barrel. For example, if the barrel is empty at the end and does not have the lulav in it, it is mentioned in the head of the section that it is due as a buffer. And as explained by MA in Sh. Not when he holds the sides of the vessel or when he holds the handle of a vessel, but places his hand under its rim. And Ral Dabhani Tarti Goni by holding the sides of the vessel or in the house of the hand, surely it was not a hindrance. Nor is it a way of insulting. Rather, when I put his hands under the rim, he dished it because of insult. Etc., a model according to our versions in Thos. And almost in this way through siman 16. And L. N. K. B. 1. from Danect that they held the sides of the vessel and he did not take that he held the sides of the vessel as CEL. And R. L. according to P. B. Damperes if he grasped the sides of the vessel that came out. A.K. not Meiri K. 3 who wrote MA that he shoved the lube in the barrel and the lube reaches the end of the barrel and he held the lube found in his hand. Ao DSL for a rider who holds the sides of the vessel alone and does not have the lance in his hand 21 except in his hand D23 there is no buffer. So there is a question as to the language of the Tos. Dahlal who held the sides of the vessel (and not the Lal who were holding) since Dakai was holding the vessel alone. According to Rabbi Damiri that he also held the Lulav in his hand. Dakai on the Lolov."
