    "10:_": "East South etc. In the year 1777 I wrote the NLAD on the matter of Hanukkah candles as the opinion of clothing in the interpretation of every corner you turn, etc. only that the clothing depended on the power of man's nature to turn 20 and on the strength of this 20 also here that you have to move east north etc. We were warned that you will always take the path that is on your right in the mikvah, there is a right and a left in front of you, you will choose your right from the Hanukkah candle, you need to start immediately with the one that is more to your right, and then you must turn to the left because the candles are placed that way, but here in Luv, where you immediately have a right and a left, we have a lickah, the right is a wise heart to your right, and you go the right way, which is south, on behalf of each turn, you have to turn to the right, and bring a rai. From the perimeter of the altar that the lamb was in the south and around the priest southeast then northeast then northeast then northwest etc. This is how the circumference of the hearth will be and not thin in the view of this rather there is evidence to the contrary the same when the priest was standing on the lamb his face was to the north and his right to the east horn south as in Defirshi in Soch DF MH 1B therefore the horn took it Tal' As for the person who stands with the lulev against the east, then his right side is towards the south, he should take what is on his right side, and the nature of the person's appeals is not to blame for this, because we choose the right side immediately, and the clothing he brought from the cities of the Levites that surrounded the east and the south, etc., that it is not similar to the lulev through the Sermon on the Kabbalah. And we are not concerned with hidden things, only those that are revealed to us and to our children, because it is appropriate even in Lulav, because there is no place to change the one who deviates from our custom and changes his hand on the bottom.",
    "11:_": "Need to connect. In the B.B., in the name of Harkanti, this secret was revealed to me in a dream on the night of the 19th of the Sukkot holiday. We were staying with an Ashkenazi Hasidic A. His name was Rabbi Yitzchak. I saw in a dream that the Omnipresent wrote the name in Yod 11 and the Omnipresent removed the last HA from the 3rd letters AL. What did you do? And his species without the etrog, and I understood a dream solution 20 because all the 4 species allude to it in the Midrash 20 Akal. And 22 in the name of Ah Dam they both took in one hand 20 Harr Shlomo did not come out as Damri' in the Gm' dela Agadia etrog with them because it is written Kafot and not Kafot Akal. And these things are not clear. LD can be an etrog with them in one association, you said that it was said and palms of dates, etc. And why didn't he say it can be with them in the hand of A. Afi' if they do not make an alliance with them, but surely the union is mercifully careful that it not be with them but in the hand of A. L.L. in it and they mention in the Toss and Asher'i above how many ways you can do in the blessing that you will move on to doing it and they said that he should bless first the taking of the etrog and they did not say if we cast only We put in one hand with the Lulav everything that is possible and it will not come out by charging him with it, but it is simply certain that if we took in one hand it came out:",
    "12:א": "(1) Nutlan in memory of Alma. It would seem to me that Daino should shake because Daino is only in memory of Alma. And the Rashal wrote in Tshu'' Dehura that the Sha'at will shake as usual during the time of praise and not during the blessing, and this is how it is written in the answer from the Rial C. 19 and it will shake according to its custom during the time of praise without a blessing all the days:",
    "12:ב": "(ב) If you cut between them. From this one must learn a fee that blesses the pancreas and then see that the Hades is a soundtrack that has been described as the way above which is mentioned, and then brings him the following verse in the name of the Rebbe, who should be blessed with the taking of the Hades and we were blessed with the heart and so on, he wrote in the name of this sign, called the R",
